# Simulated IR brightness temperature (degC) — classic enhanced-IR look:
# warm ground in grayscale (dark = hot), cold convective tops through the
# cyan/green/yellow/red/magenta/white ladder. Fully opaque like real
# satellite imagery.
#
# ⚠ Keyed in CELSIUS because GDAL's GRIB driver normalizes temperature-
# typed fields K -> C on read (same behavior as t2m — see its note). If
# the first render's raw.tif stats sit near 200-320 the driver did NOT
# normalize this field and these stops need rekeying to Kelvin.
nv     0   0   0   0
-100   130 60  160 255
-85    250 250 250 255
-75    190 0   190 255
-65    235 55  40  255
-55    248 240 0   255
-45    0   195 70  255
-35    0   160 205 255
-30    224 224 230 255
-10    168 168 176 255
10     112 112 120 255
30     62  62  70  255
45     22  22  28  255
